    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0670" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/631: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gwynn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-25T12:00:00+02:00">August 25,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 25—11:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>307. My 296, August 21, 10 a.m., and Department’s 135, August 19, 10 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">p.m</hi>.] I presented at 11 this morning the
                    informal <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to the Lebanese Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs, Philippe Boulos. He said he hoped to be able to reply soon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gwynn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
